## Commands

- `protoboard check` — resolve and run all validators (nonzero on errors)
- `protoboard inspect [stack/fc]` — context for the system or one instance
- `protoboard build` — `.protoboard/build/resolved.json` and the UHD bundle
- `protoboard parts search <words>` / `parts add <id>[@rev]` — find and
  vendor catalog parts (needs the parts service: `cloud.url` in protoboard.config.ts, or `PROTOBOARD_CLOUD_URL`;
  `protoboard login` signs in); `parts update` shows what the catalog
  recommends, `parts update <id> --to <rev>` re-pins deliberately. Nothing
  else talks to the service: check, build and inspect work offline.
- `protoboard doctor` — extensions, tools (build123d for the CAD providers), runtimes, skills
- `protoboard tools install cad` — once per checkout: the Python runtime
  with build123d that ext-frame-cad and ext-harness-cad use
- `protoboard dev` — the UHD viewer on this project, live
- `protoboard skills` — the installed skills; `protoboard skills read <name>`
  prints one; `protoboard skills export --host all` copies them to
  `.claude/skills/` and lists them in this file.
  **build-a-project** is the top-level procedure: the order of work from
  the brief to a release, one level of detail at a time
- `protoboard extensions add <name>` — add an extension (listed, linked from
  this machine's Protoboard, its skills exported)
- `protoboard run harness-cad`, `run frame-cad` — routed cables and plates
  (need Python with build123d); `run betaflight-cli` — the flight
  controller's configuration (@protoboardai/ext-drone); `run bom`
- `protoboard release --check`, then `protoboard release` — the
  Manufacturing Package (units: the flight stack, then final assembly)

Add `--format json` for machine output.

## Rules

- Cite sources for every value; mark assumptions as `assumption` traits.
- Never edit anything under `parts/catalog/`; derive a local variant with its own id.
- Never edit generated files (CAD outputs, `firmware/`, `docs/bom.*`); change
  the model and re-run the operation.
- Under `.protoboard/` everything is generated except `.protoboard/display.json`,
  the diagram's layout, which you may write (The diagram's layout, above).
- Never tell the person to run npm in the project; ask before a project-local
  install (Protoboard on this machine, above).
- Never put the parts service's token in a file.
- Model checks passing is not flight readiness.
